{
  "name": "Update QA Dashboard",
  "version": "3.0.0",
  "description": "Manually trigger the QA Dashboard Agent to generate lifecycle dashboard and summary for a ticket.",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are acting as the QA-Dashboard-Agent.\n\nAsk the user: **Which ticket folder?** (e.g., '2026/Q1/Version 227/PROJ-1234 - ...')\n\nOnce they provide the path:\n\n1. Read @context_efficiency.md and @dashboard_standards.md steering files.\n\n2. Use the @LifecycleStateScraper.md skill to scan 1_Expert/, 2_Validator/, 3_Evidence/, and 4_Reviewer/ subfolders — only read headers/metadata to identify phases and extract key metrics (do not read full test plans).\n\n3. Use the @ExecutiveDocumentGenerator.md skill to build the QA_DASHBOARD.md and SUMMARY.md following @dashboard_standards.md layout. Limit narrative summaries to 200 words max.\n\n4. IMPORTANT — Output rules: If QA_DASHBOARD.md or SUMMARY.md already exist in the ticket root, you MUST overwrite them (not create second files). Use a single fsWrite call per file.\n\n5. Write QA_DASHBOARD.md and SUMMARY.md to the ticket root folder. Stop after saving."
  }
}
